# The one place agy's pinned release is stated. CI and deploy/Dockerfile's
# build-args both derive from exactly this file; nothing else defines
# AGY_VERSION, AGY_URL_* or AGY_SHA512_* (do not reintroduce a second
# hand-maintained copy in a GitHub Actions repository variable or
# anywhere else, the whole point of this file is that there is one).
#
# WHY PINNED: agy's --output-format json envelope contract is
# version-dependent and already changed under us once. contracts/analyze.md
# 6 step 4 was verified against 1.1.13 on 2026-08-16, assuming a
# single-document "response". Live investigation on 2026-08-22 found agy
# polluting "response" with every internal self-correction turn
# concatenated (not just the final one) whenever it needs more than one
# turn to satisfy a --json-schema constraint, which a strict single-value
# JSON decode correctly rejects. Re-testing 1.1.13, 1.1.15 (this pin's
# immediate predecessor, live on ghcr since 2026-08-19) and 1.1.18 found
# the SAME defect in all three, and a separate "structured_output" field
# that is clean in every sample taken, including the failure cases; that
# is what analyzer-structured-output (a separate branch/PR) now prefers
# instead of parsing "response". Pinning does not fix this defect (it is
# present in every version tested); what it buys
# is that the next agy release is a deliberate, reviewed version bump
# with a diff, not a silent change discovered by an operator reading
# fallback logs on a rebuilt image, and it stops today's problem from
# also becoming tomorrow's "which version were we even running" question.
#
# BUMPING THIS PIN: run deploy/agy-build-args.sh to resolve the vendor's
# current release (it never writes this file, it only prints the
# build-args for a human to review), verify the printed sha512 against a
# manual download if you do not already trust the vendor manifest, then
# update the five values below together. A version bump is a contracts/
# analyze.md 6 step 4 change, not a dependency bump: re-run the same
# empirical envelope check (rich facts forcing multiple internal turns,
# a schema violation agy corrects, one it cannot correct, minimal facts
# needing one turn) before merging. The vendor publishes no changelog or
# release-notes entry for envelope/interface behaviour specifically (checked
# `agy changelog` and https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/
# blob/main/CHANGELOG.md as of 1.1.18); the CLI's general CHANGELOG is the
# closest thing to an upstream signal and does not mention this.
AGY_VERSION=1.1.18
AGY_URL_AMD64=https://storage.googleapis.com/antigravity-public/antigravity-cli/1.1.18-6435547766456320/linux-x64/cli_linux_x64.tar.gz
AGY_SHA512_AMD64=26e93eed64aa543d421a6ae9908e52ad406e8bc69f0ad9cfb7d7d14160f28841ecbb9ec07747299eea271581ab6065eee4d8e082b8144cdfa0df454044107632
AGY_URL_ARM64=https://storage.googleapis.com/antigravity-public/antigravity-cli/1.1.18-6435547766456320/linux-arm/cli_linux_arm64.tar.gz
AGY_SHA512_ARM64=fa20f794c32d6485ef001bbc7cf60d8f8be57b941b2f8dbbe20cfce4b9070e863685505a6d1e050dbff78fe412287ca02bcf7d57cfacdbe8cb1a45ebb3baf318
